  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Using UI Buttons allows for more complex behavior. One such behavior is passing around a gameobject with an onEnable trigger to change the action for a button without replacing the button. (Simplifying it here) \nDoing this on live works, but on beta this will end up breaking the trigger and then break the parent. \n\nIn the example below, there are two buttons. The left performs an action, but by default does nothing. When you press the right button it enables a sphere, and allows the left button to turn it off. \nWhen you press these buttons the first time, it works. The second time, the child object gets a Deferred event warning and does not activate. The third time, both the child and the parent get the deferred event warning and do not activate. Deferred event warnings no longer show in 614 though.\n\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/449386885299830794/480176231694991410/Broken_triggers_on_reparent.unitypackage",
